\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.10}{\ignorespaces Experimental optical configurations of the aerospike campaign. $l$ is the defocus distance, $l_{eff}$ the effective lever arm, $d_f$ the distance from the camera lens to the in-focus plane, $M_{ag}$ the magnification measured with the calibration plate, $L_{FoV_{obj}}$ the field of view at the model and $\Delta t_{exp}$ is the exposure time with which the images were captured. $S = l_{eff} \cdot M_{ag}$ is the sensitivity, $s_{min}$ the minimum distinguishable feature, $\Delta s$ the speckle size and $NPR$ the nozzle pressure ratio. ``Negative'' and ``Positive'' denote the in-focus plane lying respectively in front of or behind the model, while ``Inside TS'' denotes the focal plane inside the test section}}{63}{table.caption.63}\protected@file@percent }
